WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.520
From Kal-El to Weapon X, some fans are fan-casting
the future of their favorite actor.

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.920
While "Man of Steel" was a divisive film,
many would agree that Henry Cavill made for

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.520
an excellent Superman.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.059
Not only did he look great in the famous costume,
he also seemed to embody the character perfectly.

00:00:11.059 --> 00:00:15.130
As a result, fans have begged to see more
of Cavill as Superman.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:19.720
He's popped up in other projects since, like
"Batman v. Superman: Dawn of Justice" and

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.120
"Justice League," but he's not had the chance
to lead another solo project yet.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.950
Since "Man of Steel" came out in 2013, Warner
Bros. has been silent regarding whether we'll

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:32.750
see Cavill suit up as the Last Son of Krypton
ever again.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:37.550
Even when Superman appeared in the final episode
of "Peacemaker" Season 1, a different actor

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.690
slipped into Cavill's iconic suit, and his
face was never shown.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:46.320
And when Superman briefly appeared in "Shazam!,"
Cavill was nowhere in sight, either.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.890
There's a good chance we'll never see Cavill
as the Man of Steel ever again, but it's undeniable

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.540
that the actor is immensely talented.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.760
In fact, many fans have been left wondering
if Cavill might jump ship to Marvel.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.550
Some have even speculated that he could appear
as Captain Britain at some point in the future.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.619
Plus, one artist has imagined what the actor
could look like as one of the most iconic

00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:08.900
characters in all of Marvel Comics, and that's
Wolverine.

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:10.979
For years, Hugh Jackman was Wolverine.

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:14.750
The "X-Men" franchise went through various
iterations, but the one constant was that

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:18.100
you could always expect Jackman to show up
and lay down the hurt.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.729
Now that Disney owns 20th Century Studios,
fans are eagerly awaiting an announcement

00:01:22.729 --> 00:01:26.750
about when we'll see a new Wolverine actor
rise up and take the reins.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.070
There's a lot of talk about who could feasibly
take on such an iconic role, and Henry Cavill's

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.049
name comes up from time to time.

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:37.380
Instagram artist @royy_ledger has even taken
it upon themselves to envision what Cavill

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.520
could theoretically look like in the role,
and the result is pretty epic.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.590
Whereas Jackman's Wolverine was rough but
reasonably put together, Ledger's version

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:50.219
is positively feral, sporting the character's
iconic sideburns from the comics, as well

00:01:50.219 --> 00:01:53.529
as an incredible mask that Jackman didn't
wear during his run.

00:01:53.529 --> 00:01:57.889
It certainly seems to have won over fans as
plenty of people have commented, voicing their

00:01:57.889 --> 00:01:59.399
support for the artwork.

00:01:59.399 --> 00:02:01.229
For instance, one fan enthused,

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.299
"Definitely the BEST fan art out there ever
since this rumor came out."

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:07.229
"Tough image to shake."

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:11.700
Still, others think Cavill would be better
suited for a different mutant, with one fan

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.930
bluntly writing,

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:16.110
"Nope way [too] tall, and he's better for
cyclops I think."

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:20.390
Regardless of his next role, it's clear that
most fans just want to see Cavill appear in

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.740
another superhero property, sooner rather
than later.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:27.530
It may be a while until we get another Wolverine
introduced on film.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:32.520
Marvel Studios has yet to announce any upcoming
"X-Men" projects, despite having the rights

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:33.520
to the characters.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.690
There's no doubt that when Wolverine's time
comes, it will be one of the most hotly sought-after

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.890
roles in Hollywood.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.230
The question then becomes is Cavill the right
actor for the job?

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:46.830
Whether Wolverine makes his debut in a movie
or a Disney+ original series, there are plenty

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:50.520
of qualities Cavill could bring to the part
that make him an ideal choice.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.170
For starters, he's an incredible actor, as
evidenced by a litany of eclectic parts in

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:58.150
the likes of "The Witcher" and "Mission: Impossible
- Fallout."

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:03.080
Plus, Cavill has experience playing both good
guys and bad guys, so he could embody both

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.550
the heroic and antiheroic qualities of the
character.

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:08.360
"Be their hero.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.170
Be their monument.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.430
Be their angel.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.720
Be anything they need you to be."

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:18.470
Whether or not Cavill would be a good fit
for the role really depends on what iteration

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.740
of Wolverine the MCU goes with.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.300
In the comics, Wolverine is supposed to be
around 5'2" or 5'3".

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:29.040
Henry Cavill stands at 6'1", so he's quite
a bit taller than the character.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.600
Granted, Hugh Jackman was also taller than
Wolverine's suggested height, but the MCU

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:37.120
might want to make their next adaptation more
accurate to the comics.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.861
There's also the question of whether or not
Cavill would have time to join the MCU in

00:03:40.861 --> 00:03:45.069
such a major capacity with his prominent role
in Netflix's "The Witcher."

00:03:45.069 --> 00:03:49.690
Only time will tell, but there's no doubt
that the MCU would benefit greatly from Cavill's

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.090
presence.

